---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('tabloom')!;
const lastUpdated = 'August 21, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="How Tabloom handles account, notebook, archive, AI, and offline-reading data."
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/tabloom.png"
  socialImageAlt="Tabloom app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/tabloom">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles information
      in {app.name}, a private notebook workspace with sharing, archive, AI
      assistance, and explicit offline reading.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> Microsoft identity services provide
        the stable account identifier and basic profile details, such as name
        and email address, needed to create and secure the account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Notebook content.</strong> Notebooks, pages, rich-text blocks,
        tags, links, media, shares, versions, archive state, Inkbox scans, and
        generated content are stored so Tabloom can organize, search, share,
        restore, and return the workspace.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Operational records.</strong> Request timing, errors, AI usage
        and quota records, version information, and security events are processed
        as needed to run, secure, recover, and troubleshoot the service.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Tabloom does not use third-party advertising or cross-app tracking and
      does not need precise location, contacts, or advertising identifiers.
    </p>

    <h2>AI and embedding processors</h2>
    <p>
      Different features use different configured processors:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Anthropic Claude processes selected text, retrieved note context, or a
        chosen scan when you use summarizing, rewriting, Ask Your Notes, tag or
        notebook suggestions, or related assistance.
      </li>
      <li>
        Voyage AI creates semantic-search embeddings from page text and search
        queries when semantic search is enabled. The resulting vectors are stored
        with the private workspace.
      </li>
      <li>
        A configured Azure AI image service may process a scan selected for
        Inkbox image cleanup or extraction.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Content needed for the chosen operation is sent to the relevant provider.
      Provider processing follows that provider’s applicable service terms; this
      policy does not promise controls beyond the configuration actually
      deployed.
    </p>

    <h2>Server storage</h2>
    <p>
      Account notebooks, pages, tags, archive state, and generated content are
      stored in a private per-user SQLite database hosted on Microsoft Azure.
      Media may use account-scoped Azure storage. Information is encrypted in
      transit using HTTPS, and service access is limited to what is needed to
      operate and secure Tabloom.
    </p>

    <h2>Offline reading and IndexedDB</h2>
    <p>
      Tabloom is installable but is not local-first. When you explicitly download
      a notebook, or when the bounded recent-page setting keeps an eligible page,
      sanitized read-only copies are stored in identity-scoped IndexedDB in the
      browser profile. The service worker caches only the public shell and static
      assets; it does not cache authenticated API responses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Offline copies can include selected notebooks, pages, and optional eligible
      images within configured limits. Editing, creation, deletion, sharing,
      scanning, AI, Search, Inbox, Trash, live History, and server-backed settings
      remain unavailable offline. Reconnecting stays read-only until a complete
      authoritative refresh succeeds.
    </p>
    <p>
      IndexedDB copies are not end-to-end encrypted. Anyone with access to the
      browser profile may be able to read them, and the browser may evict them.
      Tabloom clears private offline stores when the active identity changes and
      blocks sign-out if that privacy clear fails.
    </p>

    <h2>Archive, retention, and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Archiving hides a page or notebook tree from the active workspace but does
      not delete it; archived content remains stored so an authorized owner can
      restore it. We retain account data while the account is active and as
      needed for recovery, security, or legal obligations. To request access to
      or deletion of account-associated data, email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing and service providers</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information. Microsoft provides identity and Azure
      hosting or storage. The AI and embedding providers described above process
      content only for their part of the selected or configured feature.
      Information may also be disclosed where required by law or needed to
      protect the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed
      to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when the service or its data practices change.
      The “Last updated” date above identifies the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
